      "section_path": [
        "Authentication Troubleshooting",
        "Session recovery"
      ],
      "text": "If a new session resolves HTTP 401, the earlier session likely expired. Sessions expire after 30 minutes idle or 12 hours from sign-in. A recurring 401 immediately after sign-in may indicate blocked first-party cookies or a stale organizational login route. Use a supported browser and permit the organization's required first-party session cookies. Do not disable browser security globally.",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "heading_level": 2,
      "is_semantic": true,
      "list_level": null,
      "location": {
        "bbox": null,
        "element": 16,
        "line": null,
        "page": null,
        "part": null
      },
      "marker": null,
      "ordered": null,
      "rows": null,
      "section_path": [
        "Authentication Troubleshooting",
        "MFA and lockout"
      ],
      "text": "MFA and lockout",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "heading_level": null,
      "is_semantic": true,
      "list_level": null,
      "location": {
        "bbox": null,
        "element": 17,
        "line": null,
        "page": null,
        "part": null
      },
      "marker": null,
      "ordered": null,
      "rows": null,
      "section_path": [
        "Authentication Troubleshooting",
        "MFA and lockout"
      ],
      "text": "Authenticator codes contain six digits and rotate every 30 seconds. Set automatic device time and use the next newly generated code once. Five failed password attempts within 15 minutes trigger a 30-minute lockout. Wait for the lockout to end rather than creating a series of reset requests. A password reset link lasts 20 minutes and is invalidated when a newer link is requested. AUTH-410 means the reset link has expired or been replaced.",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "heading_level": 2,
      "is_semantic": true,
      "list_level": null,
      "location": {
        "bbox": null,
        "element": 18,
        "line": null,
        "page": null,
        "part": null
      },
      "marker": null,
      "ordered": null,
      "rows": null,
      "section_path": [
        "Authentication Troubleshooting",
        "Escalation and disabled accounts"
      ],
      "text": "Escalation and disabled accounts",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "heading_level": null,
      "is_semantic": true,
      "list_level": null,
      "location": {
        "bbox": null,
        "element": 19,
        "line": null,
        "page": null,
        "part": null
      },
      "marker": null,
      "ordered": null,
      "rows": null,
      "section_path": [
        "Authentication Troubleshooting",
        "Escalation and disabled accounts"
      ],
      "text": "Lost MFA enrollment requires HR identity verification before an administrator resets it. An AUTH-DISABLED account must be reviewed by HR; support cannot infer employment status or reverse deactivation. For persistent failures, submit browser and application versions, the error code, event time with timezone, and whether a fresh session worked. Never submit a password, MFA code, reset link, session cookie, or recovery secret. Support Escalation & Security Incidents applies if an unexpected authentication event suggests unauthorized access rather than an ordinary login failure.",
      "type": "paragraph"
    }
  ],
